    "proof_tex": "On \\(I\\times S\\), treatment is absent by \\(\\mathrm{ass:window\\mbox{-}after\\mbox{-}preperiod}\\), \\(\\mathrm{ass:common\\mbox{-}start\\mbox{-}mask}\\), and causal consistency. Thus\n\\[\n Y^{\\mathrm{obs}}_{I\\times S}=M_{I\\times S}+\\epsilon_{I\\times S}.\n\\tag{33}\n\\]\nThe preperiod Gram lower bound and exact rank imply\n\\(\\sigma_r(M_{I\\times S})\\ge c\\psi\\). Applying the trace-moment calculation (3) to the full preperiod rectangle gives\n\\[\n \\|\\epsilon_{I\\times S}\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}=O_{\\mathbb P}(\\sqrt{n\\ell_n})=o_{\\mathbb P}(\\psi).\n\\tag{34}\n\\]\nUse the resolvent expansion (16)--(17) for \\(\\mathcal P_r\\) at \\(M_{I\\times S}\\). The rowwise linear term is the sum of a rank-\n\\(r\\) projection of one noise row and a left-space average across independent rows. From (2), finite \\(q\\), and a union bound over \\(N=O(n)\\) rows,\n\\[\n \\max_{i\\in I}m^{-1/2}\n \\|[D\\mathcal P_r(M_{I\\times S})\\epsilon_{I\\times S}]_{i,S}\\|_2\n =O_{\\mathbb P}(\\ell_n/\\sqrt n).\n\\tag{35}\n\\]\nThe rowwise versions of (16)--(17), (34), and the signal envelope bound the quadratic and integral terms by \\(O_{\\mathbb P}(\\ell_n^2/\\sqrt n)\\). Combining this with (35) proves\n\\[\n \\delta_{\\mathrm{fit}}le C_{\\mathbb P}\\ell_n^2/\\sqrt n.\n\\tag{36}\n\\]\n\nPut \\(d_{is}=\\widehat M^{\\mathrm{pre}}_{is}-M_{is}\\) and define the oracle product average\n\\[\n \\widetilde\\gamma(h)=\\{N(m-|h|)\\}^{-1}\n \\sum_{i=1}^N\\sum_{s:s+|h|\\in S}\\epsilon_{is}\\epsilon_{i,s+|h|}.\n\\]\nThe products have a fixed dependence range no larger than \\(2q+|h|\\) and uniformly bounded sub-exponential moments by (2). Coloring time into a fixed number of classes and applying the exponential Markov inequality to the product moments gives\n\\[\n |\\widetilde\\gamma(h)-\\gamma(h)|\n =O_{\\mathbb P}\\!\\left(\n \\sqrt{\\frac{\\log n}{m}}+\\frac{\\log n}{m}\\right)\n\\tag{37}\n\\]\nuniformly over the finitely many \\(|h|\\le q\\); this bound is conservative because it does not use the additional pooling over \\(N\\).\n\nExpanding \\(\\widehat e_{is}=\\epsilon_{is}-d_{is}\\) gives exactly\n\\[\n \\widehat\\gamma(h)-\\widetilde\\gamma(h)\n =-\\overline{d_s\\epsilon_{s+|h|}}\n  -\\overline{\\epsilon_s d_{s+|h|}}\n  +\\overline{d_sd_{s+|h|}},\n\\tag{38}\n\\]\nwhere each bar denotes the same normalized row--time average as above. Cauchy--Schwarz, (36), and the uniform boundedness in probability of the average noise square yield\n\\[\n |\\overline{d_s\\epsilon_{s+|h|}}|\n +|\\overline{\\epsilon_s d_{s+|h|}}|=O_{\\mathbb P}(\\delta_{\\mathrm{fit}}),\n \\qquad\n |\\overline{d_sd_{s+|h|}}|=O_{\\mathbb P}(\\delta_{\\mathrm{fit}}^2).\n\\tag{39}\n\\]\nEquations (37)--(39) prove the claimed covariance rate and, because \\(q\\) is fixed, the maximum-lag rate.",
